The reports in [the original incident](/kb/incidents/4471) describe bookings on the wrong
date. Two parts of the booking flow can cause that symptom. They need separate fixes.

## What the desk found

- **Shared parser.** The parser reads the month first even when the tenant writes the day
  first. It can interpret an intended 7 April as 4 July. Read the date in the tenant's format.
- **Booking-v3 date hint.** The form tells people to enter `MM/DD/YYYY` even when it reads
  their input day first. A customer following that hint can type `04/07/2026` for 7 April
  and get 4 July. Make the hint match the format the form accepts.

## Reports and scope

The table counts each report ID once and includes reports merged into #4471. It uses
the tenant's date order, booking form, and report channel to group reports. Intake tags
record the original guess from the reporter's browser. The desk's one-day-move notes
are shown within the group where those reports are filed.
The last column shows how the reports were filed in the original export.

